Description: Fits semi-parametric spatio-temporal Hawkes (self-exciting)
    point process models to event data such as crime records, using the
    stochastic-declustering expectation-maximisation (EM) approach of Zhuang
    and Mateu (2019) <doi:10.1111/rssa.12429>. The background intensity
    combines non-parametric long-term trend, weekly, monthly and spatial
    components, and the triggering kernels in time and space are
    re-estimated non-parametrically. Also provides data preparation and
    validation for 'sf' point and polygon inputs, adaptive kernel
    bandwidths, goodness-of-fit diagnostics, gridded intensity maps, and
    Monte Carlo sampling of the branching structure to quantify how events
    divide between background and triggered.
